+# Migrating to portnum v2
+
+The v2 release makes invalid port text explicit. Update imports from
+`example.com/portnum` to `example.com/portnum/v2`, including the module path in
+your `go.mod` if this module is your own module.
+
+`Parse` now returns `(int, error)` instead of a single `int`. Check the error
+before using the port:
+
+```go
+port, err := portnum.Parse(text)
+if err != nil {
+	return err
+}
+usePort(port)
+```
+
+Parsing accepts one or more ASCII decimal digits, including leading zeros, and
+values from 0 through 65535. Empty text, signs, whitespace, non-digits, and
+out-of-range values now return zero and a non-nil error. In v1 these failures
+returned zero without an error, which could be confused with port zero. The v2
+module does not include the old single-result API; the v1 release remains at
+`example.com/portnum`.
